 "area": "retina",
 "description": "SHARED integer-half-life DECAY PRIMITIVE (block 196000). One representation for any decaying quantity: last_refresh_epoch (integer innovation clock) + half_life (integer epochs, set INVERSELY by surprise) + freshness = Ashr(C0, IDiv(now_epoch - last_refresh_epoch, half_life)) -- the integer-EXACT x2^-k (scale2) atom read on the per-sensor epoch axis. The held surface is the FIRST consumer: the order-0 residual against the held prediction (sd_residual, an INTEGER temporal surprise |caught - obs_prev|) sets half_life (sd_gate) and gates the innovation clock; freshness (sd_freshness) precision-weights a Kalman blend of held-vs-new (sd_blend) so a STATIC cell keeps a long half-life and denoises (density accrues) while a MOVING cell's freshness collapses and it ADOPTS the new content (refreshed, not smeared) -- density and latency DECOUPLE over ONE held belief. A second consumer (sd_flag_stale) foveates by reading the exposed freshness attribute. A synthetic DecayTrace (sd_freshness_generic) is decayed by byte-structurally-identical machinery -- proving the primitive is shared, not perception-local. OFF by default: the rules need a HeldDecayParams node the measure adapter creates only on opt-in; absent it every existing path is byte-identical (held_surface.json untouched). NO Rust, NO new Term (Ashr/IDiv/Abs/IfThenElse/Max exist).",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "staleness_decay",
  "description": "Integer-half-life freshness (scale2 on the epoch axis) as a shared decay primitive; decay proportional to surprise decouples accumulation density from adopt latency in the held surface."
 },
